WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.900
Glad to have you with us on Tesla Short's time. Daily episode 500 coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:13.080
It's June 4th, 2026. Let's get into what's moving in the Tesla world today. 500 episodes,

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:19.880
what a journey, thank you. Tokio's new EV incentives could nearly have Tesla prices in the capital

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:26.380
region. New regional incentives in Tokyo target Model 3 and Model Y buyers with direct subsidies.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:33.040
Those subsidies could cut effective prices by up to 50 percent. Current high pricing has limited

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.700
volume in Japan. The change removes the main adoption barrier in the country's largest market.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.140
This story sits squarely in the business category because it shows how policy can open market access.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.480
Large subsidies can move a vehicle from niche import to mass market consideration.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.900
When purchase incentives reach a certain threshold, demand can shift quickly even in a country

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:02.540
with strong domestic automakers and limited public charging. The concrete mechanism is straight

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.860
forward because a buyer who previously faced a net price above typical Japanese sedan levels

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:14.360
now sees the Model Y land near mass market territory. That single change in effective price

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:20.340
moves the vehicle from niche import to plausible daily driver for a much larger segment of Tokio

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:27.060
households. Historical data from other markets indicates that once net prices cross this visibility line,

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:33.360
word of mouth and demonstration effects accelerate adoption faster than incremental range or feature

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.000
improvements. Tesla's vertical integration approach lets it capture more of the subsidy benefit

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:44.840
than competitors who rely on third-party suppliers and dealers. By controlling battery, software,

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:49.840
and direct sales, the company can adjust configurations and financing terms quickly when

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:56.720
policy changes occur. From policy-driven demand in Asia, we turn to unsupervised operations already

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:03.500
scaling in the United States. Tesla announced an expansion of its unmanned robot taxi operations across

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:09.940
the broader Austin metropolitan area. The move adds new service zones and increases available vehicles

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:16.200
without requiring safety drivers. This builds on the initial limited rollout and tests scaling under

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:23.160
current Texas regulations. The expansion gives Tesla more real world unsupervised miles in a single

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:30.160
metro region than most competitors currently operate. Next data point to watch is whether ride volumes

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:37.080
grow measurably in the new zones. While robot taxis test volume growth, another market shows what strong

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:44.300
demand looks like today. The Model Y overtook all other vehicles including domestic brands in overall

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:50.280
South Korean sales for May. Strong demand for the refreshed model and competitive pricing drove

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:57.120
the result despite import tariffs. Tesla has now led imported vehicle sales for four consecutive months.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:03.900
The outcome shows the Model Y can compete on price and features even in a market long dominated by

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:10.640
local manufacturers. Future months will reveal whether the lead holds as competitors respond. Strong

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:17.340
sales momentum in Asia contrasts with a legal setback closer to home. A new class action lawsuit alleges

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:23.080
that heat pump defects in certain Model Y and Model 3 vehicles have caused up to $400 million

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:29.780
in repair and replacement costs for Quebec owners. The filing claims Tesla knew of the issue but did not

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:35.980
disclose it at sale. This marks the fourth class action against the company in the province. Tesla has

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:42.140
not yet filed a formal response. The case will test how Canadian courts handle systemic component

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:48.140
claims across large vehicle fleets. The suit adds to existing scrutiny of component durability

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:53.680
in cold weather markets and may influence warranty reserves if similar claims spread.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:04:00.040
Legal exposure on hardware durability leads to questions about residual values on new platforms.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:07.980
Some early cyber truck reservations originally priced near $150,000 are now appearing in used listings

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:14.080
at less than half that amount. The drop reflects both expanded production of lower trim variants

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:20.860
and softening demand for the highest spec foundation series. Dealers report longer inventory dwell

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:27.200
times on loaded examples. The price compression shows how quickly Tesla's own volume ramp can affect

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.920
residual values on new platforms. Watch resale data over the next quarter to see if the trend

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:39.300
stabilizes. Production scale is reshaping truck values while elsewhere it is reshaping manufacturing

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:46.280
footprints. Elon Musk stated that the planned TerraFab facility in Grimes County, Texas will become

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:52.440
the county's biggest source of tax revenue once operational. The project is tied to next-generation

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:58.660
manufacturing capacity rather than vehicle assembly. Local officials have already begun infrastructure

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:04.120
planning around the site. The announcement gives the first concrete timeline signal for when the

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:09.780
facility could contribute to the local economy. Construction milestones will be the next visible

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:16.640
markers. New capacity plans sit alongside ongoing workplace issues. Tesla has reached settlements in

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:22.480
several individual worker racism lawsuits while a larger class action case moves toward trial.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:29.080
The company has not disclosed settlement amounts. The remaining case involves allegations from multiple

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:35.740
California facilities and could set precedent for future employment claims. Tesla continues to face

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:41.940
ongoing scrutiny of workplace culture at its US plants. The outcome of the larger trial will

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:48.180
influence how similar suits are valued. Domestic labor matters give way to competitive moves by rivals.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:54.640
BYD has begun offering lifetime free battery replacements on certain models sold in China.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:06:00.560
The program is framed as a response to consumer concerns over long-term battery degradation

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:07.920
rather than a direct competitive move. Tesla has not adopted similar lifetime coverage in any market.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:14.180
The difference highlights contrasting approaches to residual value guarantees between the two companies.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.720
Observers will track whether the policy changes BYD's used vehicle values or warranty costs.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:26.760
Competitor policy experiments contrast with second life uses already being tested elsewhere.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:33.540
Retired Waymo Robotaxi battery packs are being redeployed as stationary grid storage in pilot

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:39.740
projects. The program tests second life economics for high cycle autonomous vehicle packs.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:46.680
Tesla has discussed similar second life uses for its own packs but has not announced active grid storage

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:53.240
deployments at scale. The Waymo effort provides an early data point on degradation after intensive

00:06:53.240 --> 00:07:01.140
ride-hale duty cycles. Results could inform Tesla's own plans for 4,680 and structural pack

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:08.020
second life applications. Second life data points close the main news while quick social updates follow.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:13.460
Owners can now check cabin temperature and pet status directly from their wrist through

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:19.220
the promoted pet mode on Apple Watch. The feature pulls live data from the car's climate system

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:25.380
and sends alerts if conditions change. Tesla posted the update alongside a short video showing the

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:30.580
watch interface. It extends the existing pet mode beyond the car's screen and phone app.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:37.120
The addition makes the feature more accessible during short stops. A new video shows a Tesla robot

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:42.700
waving and appearing to smile at approaching people. The clip was posted by the official Tesla

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:49.760
account with the caption, it is just happy to see you. The motion uses existing actuator ranges rather

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:55.900
than new hardware. It is one of the first public examples of expressive movement intended for future

00:07:55.900 --> 00:08:02.400
optimus units. Observers noted the simple gesture already elicits strong viewer reactions online.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:07.420
Tesla Rattie shared a speculative rendering of a potential new Tesla model.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:14.380
The image prompted hundreds of replies debating design price and segment fit. No official confirmation

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:20.480
exists that the vehicle is in development. The post illustrates how quickly concept images can drive

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:27.240
engagement even without confirmed specs. It also shows sustained appetite for smaller or lower priced

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:34.100
Tesla options. Before we go, keep an eye on whether Austin Ride Volumes show measurable growth after

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:42.600
the latest Robo Taxi Zone expansion. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at $424.32.

